<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tripartite Pact</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1940</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Berlin Pact · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tripartite Pact was signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> on 27 September 1940 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, who pledged to assist one another if attacked by a power not yet in the war, chiefly aimed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> joined, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> signed on 25 March 1941. Two days later a military coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> overthrew the Yugoslav government, and Germany invaded the country in April.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tripartite-pact.jpg" alt="Tripartite Pact" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heinrich Hoffmann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Signing_ceremony_for_the_Axis_Powers_Tripartite_Pact.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
